== About me
I received my PhD from The University of Texas at Austin, where I was fortunate to be advised by [https://sites.google.com/view/sanjay-shakkottai/home Sanjay Shakkottai]. During my time in grad school, I was also blessed to have worked with these amazing collaborators: [https://sites.google.com/a/illinois.edu/srikant/ R. Srikant], [https://people.maths.bris.ac.uk/~maajg/ Ayalvadi Ganesh], [https://abishek90.github.io/ Abishek Sankararaman] and [https://sites.google.com/view/danielvial/ Daniel Vial]. 

My research interests lie broadly in the fields of machine learning, optimization and networks. In particular, I am interested in developing efficient and reliable machine learning tools for real-life applications, and characterizing their theoretical and empirical behavior. My PhD thesis focused on design and analysis of communication-efficient decentralized algorithms in various multi-agent bandit settings.
	
